{
  "_readme": [
    "Where the window was left, and whether that place still exists.",
    "",
    "Both backends read and write the same window.json, so they have to agree",
    "about what a half-written one means. The fallback is per field rather",
    "than all at once: a file with a good size and a nonsense position keeps",
    "the size.",
    "",
    "Everything is logical pixels. Tauri reports physical ones, so what comes",
    "off the window is divided by the scale factor before it is written -",
    "otherwise a window left at 1345 wide on a Retina display is remembered as",
    "2690 and comes back filling two of them.",
    "",
    "Run: pnpm run test (TypeScript) and cargo test (Rust). Both read this."
  ],
